Third-party components
----------------------

nextup bundles third-party packages, each under its own licence. The complete,
machine-generated inventory is `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`; it is regenerated by
`npm run notices` and CI fails if it drifts from the installed production
dependency tree (`T-LICENSE-001`).

Retained-notice obligations
---------------------------

Some components are weak copyleft (LGPL / MPL / EPL). They are used as
**unmodified, replaceable** dependencies, which does not place this MIT work
under their terms — but their licence notices are retained, and nothing in this
project prevents a user from replacing them with a modified version.

The obligation this project knowingly carries is the HEIC/HEIF decoder:

    heic-convert  (ISC)        HEIC -> PNG wrapper
    heic-decode   (ISC)        decode HEIC -> raw RGBA
    libheif-js    (LGPL-3.0)   WASM build of libheif (the codec)

`libheif-js` is used **decode-only**, so no GPL `x265` encoder and no
patent-encumbered encoder is present. The owner recorded approval of this
obligation at TASK-153; see `docs/adr/ADR-0008-heic-transcode-on-ingest.md`
and `specs/security.md` §9.

The decoder itself is added by TASK-147. Until then it is absent from the
dependency tree and therefore absent from `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`, which
lists what actually ships rather than what is planned.

